Round 5 is done: one fix to the run order, with the commit (`fd338c9`) pushed to `r2e main`.

**Current state (15:52 UTC):** the pipeline is running normally. Memory use is 12.5 GiB of the 60 GiB limit, and no processes have been killed for running out of memory.
- **Rung 0 (coordinate input):** the distillation step (copying the teacher's solutions) is at iteration 500. The mid-run check on held-out boards gives decap count relative to greedy+prune and failure rate as follows. These are not report numbers.

  | Board kind | Count vs greedy+prune | Failure rate |
  |---|---|---|
  | PCB | 2.66 | 0.62 |
  | Package | 1.50 | 0.69 |
  | Interposer | 0.77 | 0.25 |

  Log: `runs/2026-10-28/r0_coord_distill/log.txt`.
- **Evaluation boards:** 5 of the 12 sets at 10×10 and 16×16 are built. The 16×16 sets are still being built.

**Fix this round:** the controlling script was going to run the full local-search baseline before evaluating any trained rung. That baseline is slow: it re-runs greedy hundreds of times per board and starts with the largest (16×16) boards. Rung 0 finishes training around 17:40, and its evaluation would have waited behind that, possibly for hours. I haven't timed local search on 16×16 boards yet, so the length of that delay is an estimate.

The new order in `scripts/pipeline_day1.py`:
1. Run the fast baselines (greedy+prune and the modal rule) on all boards.
2. Run local search on the 10×10 boards.
3. Evaluate each rung as soon as it finishes training.
4. Run local search on the 16×16 boards one board kind at a time, only when no finished rung is waiting.

Only the order changed; the experiment settings are the same. I restarted the script at 15:49. It reconnected to the running training and board-building jobs without interrupting them. The decision and reason are recorded in PROGRESS.md.

**Next round:** record the rest of rung 0 (distillation, then reinforcement learning). Once the evaluation boards are done, put the first baseline numbers into RESULTS.md, then confirm rung 1 starts at about 19:45. DAILY.md is due around 05:30 UTC on 10/29.
